SFCM_DATA_PART("audits/recs/recs.json",8,183,{"rows":{"rows":[["K-bbd407e0d0",94,"cgj","DPH",8,8,null,"The City should develop an integrated informational system that can track participants and provide the homeless population with improved and focused services from the City and from service providers. CGJ recognizes that information sharing of this type is controversial. It is the view of the CGJ that serious consideration should be given to a system similar to DPH's 'Reggie' system... Such a...",674,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3",9,3,null,"The City has no method of tracking delivery of homeless-related social services, causing duplicate counting and poor planning; a 2004 HUD HMIS mandate looms.",7,14,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Public Health","Homelessness and Supportive Housing"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.85,"department":0.85,"category":0.9,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-84d4b06c47",94,"cgj","HOM",8,8,null,"The City and the Local Board should convene involved departments, homeless advocates, and service providers in order to develop an integrated, central database of available beds. A city-wide referral system would improve access to the location of available beds on any given night.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4a",10,3,null,"There is no integrated referral database to ascertain available shelter beds in real time.",7,14,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Homelessness and Supportive Housing"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.8,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.65},null,[]],["K-df56aabe83",94,"cgj","HOM",8,14,null,"The Local Board and City departments should develop minimum standards of operation for all homeless shelters.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4b",10,3,null,"Living conditions and standards of care vary greatly across City shelters, with no consistent minimum standards.",13,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Homelessness and Supportive Housing","Human Services Agency","Public Health"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.75,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.65},null,[]],["K-768d0e067f",94,"cgj","HOM",8,14,null,"The Local Board and City departments should develop a standard 'Bill of Rights' for all shelter participants, inform participants of these rights, and create standard system-wide operating policies.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4c",10,3,null,"There is no system-wide 'Bill of Rights' for shelter participants; rules of participation vary greatly by location.",13,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Homelessness and Supportive Housing","Human Services Agency","Public Health"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.75,"category":0.65,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.65},null,[]],["K-bb1526cde5",94,"cgj","HOM",8,7,null,"The Local Board and City departments should develop minimum standards of training for all shelter staff and establish minimum client-staff ratios throughout the entire shelter system.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4d",10,3,null,"City shelters have no established minimum client-staff ratios and varying levels of staff training.",14,14,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Homelessness and Supportive Housing","Human Services Agency","Public Health"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.75,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.65},null,[]],["K-e466f2100a",94,"cgj","HOM",8,13,null,"The Local Board and City departments should work with the Mayor's Office on Disability to ensure that all shelters, including the expanded winter shelters, are architecturally ADA compliant in addition to ensuring reasonable programmatic access at each site. In addition, CGJ recommends that the Office of Contract Administration work with the MOD to ensure that all homeless service contracts...",764,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":3,"why":null},"4e",10,3,null,"Provision of ADA programmatic access is inconsistent throughout the shelter system, and architectural access compliance is inconsistent and requires review.",12,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Homelessness and Supportive Housing","Human Services Agency","Public Health","Mayor's Office","City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.8,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.65},null,[]],["K-0dd4ed82ef",94,"cgj","HOM",8,5,null,"CGJ concurs with the Continuum of Care and strongly recommends that the Local Board and City departments convene a system-wide shelter monitoring committee to provide oversight for shelter conditions and standards of care.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4f",11,3,null,"No system-wide committee exists to monitor and oversee shelter conditions and standards of care.",5,14,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Homelessness and Supportive Housing","Human Services Agency","Public Health"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.75,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.65},null,[]],["K-c5cbe15113",94,"cgj","MYR",8,11,null,"The Mayor, Local Board, Board of Supervisors, advocates, service providers, and major City departments need to initiate a major public education effort about homelessness and the reality of poverty in San Francisco. This campaign should cover but not be limited to the historical and root causes of poverty and homelessness, the history and status of the City's past and current efforts in...",784,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"5",11,3,null,"There has been minimal public education about homelessness, its causes, and City efforts, leaving the public largely uninformed.",10,14,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Mayor's Office","Homelessness and Supportive Housing","Board of Supervisors","Human Services Agency","Public Health"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.8,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.65},null,[]],["K-db4eb4eb61",93,"cgj","BOS",8,11,null,"In the budget process, the Mayor and the Board of Supervisors should consider the total amount needed to fund all parts of the criminal justice system; increases for APD should be offset by reductions elsewhere in the criminal justice budget.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1",4,3,null,"Criminal justice system budgets are funded separately rather than through an integrated approach, despite probation's potential to reduce costs elsewhere.",10,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Board of Supervisors","Mayor's Office"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-b40e015bf8",93,"cgj","ADP",8,14,null,"The Mayor and the Board of Supervisors should support APD in accelerating a commitment toward community-located probation activities. APD should reassign probation caseloads by socioeconomic and geographic neighborhoods, based on input from the public, CBOs working with APD, and the Police Department.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2",4,3,null,"Adult probation remains centralized at the Hall of Justice (850 Bryant) despite best practices favoring community-based probation efforts.",13,11,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Adult Probation","Board of Supervisors","Mayor's Office"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-b8155e38ca",93,"cgj","ADP",8,7,null,"The Mayor and the Board of Supervisors should make a commitment to assist APD in hiring additional Spanish-speaking POs by providing additional slots that require Spanish fluency, and by allowing retirement/attrition of current probation officers to bring department staffing to its authorized level.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3",5,3,null,"San Francisco lacks sufficient bilingual Spanish-speaking probation officers relative to the number of monolingual Spanish-speaking offenders.",14,14,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Adult Probation","Board of Supervisors","Mayor's Office"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.75,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-97e037609f",93,"cgj","ADP",8,5,null,"APD and the court should adopt measures to ensure that POs and judges are, whenever possible, assigned to offenders from the time of their initial arrest through any re-offenses.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4",5,3,null,"Offenders who are re-arrested have no assurance of being assigned the same judge and probation officer as for the initial offense, harming rehabilitation continuity.",5,14,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Adult Probation","Superior Court"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.85,"category":0.6,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-ec3bc92602",90,"cgj","BOS",8,3,null,"REBUILD SAN FRANCISCO GENERAL HOSPITAL. The existence of SFGH to ensure the delivery of the best possible health care -- such as acute care services, trauma care, and wellness -- is essential to the overall quality of life in San Francisco. Rebuilding SFGH's acute hospital facilities, rather than the other available options, not only serves to maintain the highest level of health care for San...",514,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1",6,3,null,"Three SFGH buildings are rated SPC-1 and must be rebuilt, retrofitted, or cease acute care operations after 2008/2013 under state seismic law SB1953.",0,11,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Board of Supervisors","Public Health","Mayor's Office"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.8,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-3a0e657cfb",90,"cgj","DPH",8,11,null,"In order to take appropriate actions to implement the State's seismic safety mandates, San Francisco should complete a master plan for SFGH.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2a",7,3,null,"San Francisco lacks a current master plan for SFGH accounting for SB1953 seismic mandates; the most recent plan dates to 1987.",10,3,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Public Health"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.85,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-fe5a0634d0",90,"cgj","BOS",8,11,null,"QUICKLY DEVELOP A SHARED VISION AND INTRODUCE A BOND MEASURE that will have the greatest chance of voter approval. All involved parties -- the Mayor, Board of Supervisors, Health Commission, Director of Public Health -- must develop a shared vision for San Francisco's health care needs, including the location and configuration of services and the role SFGH will play in meeting those needs....",513,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2b",7,3,null,"No adequate plan exists for a bond issue to finance SFGH's seismic compliance; political considerations are delaying the timing of a bond measure.",10,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Board of Supervisors","Public Health","Mayor's Office"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.85,"category":0.8,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-826cc01446",90,"cgj","DPH",8,11,null,"MAINTAIN THE MUTUALLY BENEFICIAL SFGH-UCSF AFFILIATION. As SFGH goes forward with its plans to rebuild, it must consider seriously the requirements and needs of UCSF as they relate to research, facilities, access to patients, and compliance with UC regents' policy.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3",8,3,null,"The SFGH-UCSF affiliation, essential for staffing SFGH with quality physicians, must be preserved amid rebuilding plans and UC Regents' seismic safety requirements for research facilities.",10,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Public Health"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-4feec85310",90,"cgj","BOS",8,14,null,"EDUCATE THE PUBLIC ON THE ROLE OF SFGH IN THE COMMUNITY. Mount a public service campaign to inform the citizens of San Francisco of the significance of SFGH and its Level 1 Trauma Center in our midst.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4",9,3,null,"Many citizens may not be aware of the extent to which SFGH serves the general population, which is relevant to obtaining voter approval for funding.",13,11,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Board of Supervisors","Public Health","Mayor's Office"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.75,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.7},null,[]],["K-bd903fa705",89,"cgj","ADM",8,1,null,"The Purchasing division within the Office of Contract Administration should update Chapter 900 (Personal Services and Lease Contracts) of the \"Guide to Ordering Goods and Services\" manual to specifically address contracts under $50,000 and \"sole source\" contracts. This update should be consistent with HRC requirements.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1",2,3,2,"Purchasing regulations have not been updated since 1989 and do not reflect Charter or Code revisions, leaving no current guidance for departments on sub-$50,000 or sole source contracts.",2,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.9,"response":0.4,"target_date":0.5},null,[]],["K-a1d1a0d17a",89,"cgj","CON",8,1,null,"The Controller should conduct an audit of all Professional Services contracts below $50,000 to ensure compliance with HRC and Purchasing requirements. Special attention should be placed on public relations contracts and those contracts which have not included a well defined scope of work and where amendments subsequently include items such as printing and materials.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2",3,3,3,"Widespread practice of awarding Professional Services contracts below $50,000 without competitive solicitation or HRC review, and use of contract amendments to circumvent thresholds, especially for public relations contracts.",2,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Controller"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.9,"response":0.4,"target_date":0.5},null,[]],["K-4ad9e2e5f3",89,"cgj","CON",8,1,null,"The Controller should provide an annual report to the Mayor and to the Board of Supervisors on the number, dollar value, and rationale of \"sole source\" contracts for each department.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3",3,3,3,"Sole source exemptions are frequently declared without documented rationale, based only on validation of compliance requirements rather than the actual uniqueness criteria intended by the Code.",2,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Controller","Mayor's Office","Board of Supervisors"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.85,"category":0.9,"response":0.4,"target_date":0.5},null,[]],["K-aca049c7aa",92,"cgj","CPC",8,12,null,"Additional funds could be generated for enforcement by requiring annual renewal of permits and by inspection of existing billboard signs, with a yearly charge per sign. This would facilitate and pay for discovering sites without permits, illegally altered sites, and illegal new installations.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1",4,3,5,"CPD budget lacks a dedicated allocation for enforcement of outdoor advertising signs; fines are not a reliable funding source.",11,4,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["City Planning"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-b4e0977097",92,"cgj","CPC",8,8,null,"Assign a separate and distinct numerical designation to all existing, active, legal outdoor advertising sign permits (to distinguish them from all other sign permits) for entry into the computer system. Flag each for automatic periodic site reviews by CPD.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2a",5,3,5,"CPD and DBI electronic files cannot distinguish outdoor advertising signs from standard signs, making it impossible to accurately track legal billboards.",7,3,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["City Planning"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.85,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-086425764f",92,"cgj","CPC",8,3,null,"Conduct a city-wide count and permit history of every existing billboard sign. Many of the originally grandfathered signs (prior to 1966) have no permits on file. Researching ownership (which may have changed repeatedly over time); checking the existence of permits or verifying legal status with other evidence, such as dated photos; and entering this information into the database, under the...",151,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2b",5,3,5,"Many grandfathered signs predate reliable permit records, and CPD lacks accurate information on legal billboard status.",0,8,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["City Planning"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.75,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-99eef3a541",92,"cgj","CPC",8,7,null,"The Planning Director should hire a temporary staff person -- with special expertise to conduct a city-wide survey of all extant billboards -- to enter the information into the electronic database described Recommendation 2a. Under the direction of a professional who has knowledge of San Francisco's billboard history, collegiate Urban Planning interns who are periodically invited to train in...",810,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3",5,3,6,"CPD lacks budget and experienced staff with time to conduct a needed citywide census of billboards.",14,3,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["City Planning"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.8,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-9aa32d9276",92,"cgj","CPC",8,5,null,"CPD staff and CalTrans Right of Way staff should coordinate immediately to enforce the new ban within the 600 ft. corridor, so that no Cal Trans permits are issued. Failure to do so will cause confusion among billboard businesses and could evolve into costly regulatory procedures. Pertinent billboard census information should be shared regularly between the two agencies.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4",6,3,6,"No efficient coordination process exists between CPD and CalTrans for billboard permitting near state highways, risking conflicting permit issuance after the city ban.",5,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["City Planning","Other non-City entity"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.85,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-4d25d8eaab",92,"cgj","CPC",8,14,null,"CPD should prepare a pamphlet containing an explanation of the relevant rules for sign regulation, as well as a complaint form to help citizens identify suspected billboard signs without valid permits. That same information should be added to CPD web site.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"5",6,3,6,"No comprehensive, easily understood guide exists for laws and procedures on outdoor advertising signs, especially given the new ban.",13,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["City Planning"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-b09d670910",92,"cgj","CPC",8,14,null,"To help each CPD Quadrant Senior Planner quickly identify possible non-compliance situations, CPD should set up a 24-hour call line for billboard complaints only; this phone number should be listed in CPD's white page telephone directory. CPD should disseminate information to the public by other means, such as placing the public information pamphlet, suggested in Recommendation 5 above, in...",904,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"6",6,3,7,"Citizen complaints about illegal signs are commingled with other complaints, delaying response and allowing illegal signs to profit during delays.",13,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["City Planning"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-dede3e90a4",95,"cgj","BOS",8,5,null,"The City should immediately establish a permanent economic development and public information office, and should locate this office at the gates to the shipyard. This office should act as a clearinghouse to facilitate information and communication between employers and job seekers, and to provide referrals to sources for technical training, as well as for business education and financing. This...",675,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1",6,3,null,"RAB, CAC, and PAC lack coordinated communication, weakening information flow to the community and contributing to mistrust.",5,14,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Board of Supervisors","Economic and Workforce Development","Office of Community Investment and Infrastructure"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-1aa19be32b",95,"cgj","ECN",8,11,null,"Policies and Objectives 18 and 19 - as proposed in the HPS Area Plan of the General Plan - i.e., 'Provide employment, business and entrepreneurial opportunities for Bayview Hunters Point residents and businesses' and 'Provide education and job training opportunities for Bayview Hunter Point residents,' must be implemented. The City should ensure job availability for BVHP residents - at both...",501,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2a",6,3,null,"Insufficient assurances that BVHP residents will benefit from jobs, contracts, and ownership opportunities from HPS development.",10,14,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Economic and Workforce Development","Office of Community Investment and Infrastructure"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-a2c2d0b23f",95,"cgj","ECN",8,11,null,"The MOA between the Navy and the City should be amended to include training and hiring for the community to ensure employment in clean-up and development activities.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2b",7,3,null,"Existing efforts to encourage local training and hiring by on-site contractors are insufficient.",10,7,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Economic and Workforce Development"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.95,"department":0.9,"category":0.6,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-f34f9a4d41",95,"cgj","ENV",8,13,null,"DPH should review what testing and monitoring of the HPS site has been completed or is underway, and should identify what additional evaluations must be made. Using federal and state expertise and information, the City should work with the Navy and environmental regulators to review available test data in determining whether collection, ventilation, and/or treatment systems are warranted at...",225,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":3,"why":null},"3",7,3,null,"Lack of agreement among agencies on health hazards at HPS and incomplete site characterization contribute to community mistrust.",12,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Environment","Public Health","Economic and Workforce Development","Office of Community Investment and Infrastructure"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.85,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-65e0f2f04c",95,"cgj","ENV",8,0,null,"DEnv, MOED, and SFRA should require that new businesses in HPS comply with all environmental regulations, and the City should strictly enforce compliance (including imposing monetary penalties). The City and the community must be assured that the legacy of toxic contamination at HPS is not repeated. All proposed reuses, both residential and industrial, must be required by the City to commit to...",216,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4",8,3,null,"Need to prevent repeat of past environmental degradation as HPS transitions to civilian reuse.",1,13,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,3,["Environment","Economic and Workforce Development","Office of Community Investment and Infrastructure"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.75,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.6},null,[]],["K-5e03495b5d",776,"csa","BOS",10,1,null,"To ensure fiscal propriety and responsibility, the Board of Supervisors should amend the Administrative Code, Chapter 21, by adding a definition of a sole source contract.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1",18,0,null,"There is no legal definition of a sole source contract in the City Charter or Administrative Code, creating ambiguity in contracting decisions.",2,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.8,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-5780ca7f9a",776,"csa","ADM",10,1,null,"The Office of Contract Administration should change its procedures to require departments to submit all existing sole source contracts for professional services for review within a reasonable time period so that existing contracts can be reviewed under its new guidelines.",null,"agree","OCA agrees with the audit's assessment that the City's past approach to sole source contracting was inadequate.",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2",8,0,34,"Existing sole source contracts predating new OCA guidelines have not been reviewed under the new standards.",2,null,null,765,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.85,"response":0.5,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-a87c8ac7f0",776,"csa","ADM",10,1,null,"The Office of Contract Administration should work with departments to help them understand the Office of Contract Administration's new requirements and the procedures they must follow to comply with them.",null,"agree","OCA agrees with the audit's assessment that the City's past approach to sole source contracting was inadequate.",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3",9,2,34,"Departments may not fully understand new OCA sole source waiver requirements and procedures.",2,null,null,765,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.8,"response":0.5,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-0db3b6d659",776,"csa","ADM",10,1,null,"The Office of Contract Administration should make the new procedures add value to the contracting process by seeking input from departmental and other users through periodic evaluations, customer satisfaction surveys, or focus group discussions.",null,"agree","OCA agrees with the audit's assessment that the City's past approach to sole source contracting was inadequate.",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4",10,2,34,"There is no mechanism to gather feedback on whether the new sole source procedures are effective and add value.",2,10,null,765,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.75,"response":0.5,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-7267422b92",776,"csa","ADM",10,8,null,"The Office of Contract Administration should develop a computerized, sole source database that includes all relevant information for each contract, including type of contract, contracting department, name of contractor, award amount, term of contract, summary of work to be performed, and other relevant information. The database should also have the capability to produce summary reports that...",799,"agree","OCA has developed a tracking system for all sole source contracts that come through its office (currently paper-based).",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"5",10,2,34,"The City has no comprehensive, reliable, computerized data on the number or value of its sole source contracts.",7,1,null,769,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.85,"response":0.55,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-83c4e929e2",776,"csa","ADM",10,10,null,"The Office of Contract Administration should ensure that it can produce the types of reports that the Board of Supervisors, other City officials, or the public may request, by making inquiries with individuals, departments, Board members and others on what they want to know about sole source contracts.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"6",10,2,null,"OCA lacks a mechanism to determine what reporting outputs stakeholders need regarding sole source contracts.",9,8,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.85,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.5,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-ac2a3dfd69",776,"csa","CON",10,8,null,"To enable the City to capture information on all sole source contracts for professional services, the Controller should modify the City's Financial Accounting Management Information System (FAMIS) to include a required field that indicates whether or not a contract is a sole source contract.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,198,0.8,null,{"score":3,"why":"Repeats an earlier recommendation to the same department."},"7",19,0,null,"FAMIS does not currently record whether a contract is a sole source contract, preventing citywide reporting.",7,null,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Controller"],null,null,343,"C-0473",{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.9,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-4e1f1a4f84",776,"csa","BOS",10,0,null,"The Clerk of the Board of Supervisors should request in its next letter to all City departments that they submit lists of all their existing sole source contracts to the Clerk, or report that they have no sole source contracts.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"8",19,0,null,"Only 19 of 66 City departments reported sole source contracts as required under the Sunshine Ordinance for fiscal year 2001-02.",1,1,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.75,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-f84c8553e1",776,"csa","BOS",10,5,null,"The Clerk of the Board of Supervisors should report to the Board of Supervisors on the extent to which departments have complied with the ordinance.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"9",10,2,null,"No compiled information is provided to the Board on department compliance with the sole source reporting requirement.",5,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.75,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-2b0d73646e",776,"csa","AIR",10,1,null,"To avoid awarding City funds or contracts to specific contractors without using competitive processes, the Airport should competitively solicit for consultants for municipal bond financing and for firms that provide proficiency testing for communications dispatchers as soon as possible.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"10",30,0,null,"Two Airport contracts (with John F. Brown and Deltronics) have existed for over 14 years without competitive solicitation or sole source waivers.",2,null,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Airport"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.9,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.6},false,[]],["K-62021a53dd",776,"csa","DPH",10,1,null,"To avoid awarding City funds or contracts to specific contractors without using competitive processes, the Department of Public Health, Office of Contract Management, should begin competitive solicitation processes for its contractually delivered services for which it has not competitively solicited in the last 10 or more years.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"11",30,0,null,"DPH reported 89 contracts under contract for the same service for at least 10 years without competitive solicitation.",2,null,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Public Health"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.9,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-f5c0af5b46",776,"csa","DPH",10,1,null,"The Department of Public Health, Office of Contract Management, should obtain a sole source waiver from the Office of Contract Administration for contracts where the funding source designates a particular provider and for contracts that are otherwise sole source contracts.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"12",21,2,null,"Some DPH long-term contracts lack required sole source waivers despite being effectively sole source in nature.",2,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Public Health"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.85,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-678092f60a",776,"csa","BOS",10,5,null,"The Board of Supervisors should no longer direct funds toward specific City contracts or contractors through the addback process or otherwise. This includes no longer adding additional money to existing contracts, and no longer earmarking funds for specific new contractors. The Board may appropriately allocate funds to nonprofit organizations by budgeting those funds to departments that will...",647,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"13",30,0,null,"The Board's addback practice of earmarking funds for specific organizations violates the Charter's non-interference provision and circumvents competitive solicitation.",5,1,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.8,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-be4987e5c1",776,"csa","BOS",10,1,null,"The Board of Supervisors should competitively solicit to select its budget analyst.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"14",21,2,null,"The Board has engaged the same budget analyst (Harvey Rose) for over 24 years without competitive solicitation.",2,null,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.9,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-0bd696ea20",776,"csa","BOS",10,0,null,"The Board of Supervisors should consider amending the language in Administrative Code Section 21.9 to state that the terms of the contract, including options to renew, must be stated in both the solicitation and the contract.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"15",21,2,null,"Some City contracts omit contract term and renewal conditions, increasing risk of improper renewal beyond allowed limits.",1,1,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.75,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-fbabd56fed",776,"csa","MYR",10,5,null,"To avoid awarding City funds or contracts to specific contractors without using competitive processes, the Mayor's Office should no longer use technical adjustments or other enhancements to the City's annual budget to add back funds to specific organizations.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"16",30,0,null,"The Mayor's Office allocated over $1.4 million in FY2002-03 to 27 specific organizations through technical budget adjustments, bypassing competition.",5,1,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Mayor's Office"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.75,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-cffc8f8dc9",776,"csa","CITYWIDE",10,1,null,"All departments should familiarize themselves with the new procurement guidelines from the Office of Contract Administration and check their files to bring all outstanding contracts into compliance, if necessary, by using competitive solicitation when the current contracts expire.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"17",31,0,null,"Departments may not be fully aware of new OCA sole source guidelines, risking noncompliant contracts.",2,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Citywide"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.8,"category":0.8,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-306b82d3d7",776,"csa","CITYWIDE",10,1,null,"All departments should always include complete contract terms including options to renew (number of renewals and length of each renewal) and conditions for renewal in the contract.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"18",22,2,null,"Several City contracts reviewed lacked stated contract terms or renewal conditions, complicating enforcement of the 10-year renewal limit.",2,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Citywide"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.8,"category":0.8,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-dec5d57875",776,"csa","CITYWIDE",10,1,null,"Before the contract expires, all departments should again use a competitive process to select the provider of the services for the next period (unless the contract is an exception to the competitive solicitation process). Contracts should not be renewed beyond the contract term, including renewal periods, as listed in the solicitation document and contract.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"19",22,2,null,"Contracts have been renewed beyond stated terms without a new competitive process.",2,null,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Citywide"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.8,"category":0.85,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-827ad29f4c",776,"csa","CAT",10,0,null,"To ensure that contracts protect the City's interests, the City Attorney should review all pending City contracts to make sure that the proper dates and renewal terms are clearly and properly stated in the original contract.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"20",31,0,null,"The City Attorney's contract review does not currently verify that solicitation terms match contract terms for dates and renewals.",1,1,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Attorney"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.85,"response":0.6,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-688744544a",776,"csa","ADM",10,5,null,"To establish an efficient approval path for the City's sole source contracts, the Office of Contract Administration should adapt its procedures to include notifying the Human Rights Commission of its decision to approve sole source contract waivers so that the Human Rights Commission may work with departments to bring sole source vendors into compliance with the City's human rights laws.",null,"agree","OCA states it will continue to work with HRC and other departments to solve the issues addressed in the audit.",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"21",31,0,34,"Lack of coordination between OCA and HRC on sole source waiver approvals creates inefficiency and duplicated review.",5,1,null,770,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.85,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.55,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-ce96bc5ea8",776,"csa","HRC",10,5,null,"To avoid needless paperwork, gain efficiency in the contract approval process, and comply with the Administrative Code, the Human Rights Commission should not review sole source waiver requests that have been approved by the Office of Contract Administration. The Human Rights Commission should stay informed of sole source contracts so that it can continue to work with departments to try to...",899,"disagree","We respectfully disagree with your recommendations regarding HRC's role in approving sole source contracts.",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":3,"why":null},"22",31,0,38,"Both OCA and HRC separately review sole source waiver requests, creating duplicative paperwork and delays.",5,1,null,1384,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Human Rights Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.85,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-94aef51618",776,"csa","HRC",10,0,null,"The Human Rights Commission should notify all City departments that the MBE/WBE/LBE Ordinance does not require a sole source waiver for 'awards made by the City with federal/State grant or City general fund monies to a nonprofit entity where the City offers assistance, guidance, or supervision on a project or program and the recipient of the grant award uses the grant monies to provide...",759,"agree","The HRC is willing to notify departments of this distinction.",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"23",22,2,39,"Some City departments unnecessarily seek HRC approval for sole source agreements with nonprofits providing community services that are exempt from the ordinance.",1,6,null,1136,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Human Rights Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.8,"target_date":0.9},false,[]],["K-acaa7e8e5c",748,"csa","BOS",11,5,null,"Amend Charter Section 4.109 to include specific criteria for future appointments to the Police Commission to address community representation, district representation, expertise in law enforcement law, civil rights law, public safety policy and procedures, and/or expertise in handling of police disciplinary matters.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1a",6,3,null,"Police Commission appointment criteria are unspecified, weakening qualifications and accountability of appointees.",5,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Mayor's Office","Police Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.7,"category":0.8,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-c468735c5a",748,"csa","BOS",11,5,null,"Amend Charter Section 4.109 to require Board of Supervisors' approval of mayoral appointments to the Commission and of removals of any Police Commission member.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1b",6,3,null,"Mayor unilaterally appoints and removes Police Commissioners without legislative check, weakening accountability.",5,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Mayor's Office","Police Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.7,"category":0.8,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-84bba8d4ef",748,"csa","BOS",11,5,null,"Amend Charter Section 4.109 to limit Commissioners to two consecutive terms.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1c",6,3,null,"Police Commission appointments currently have no term limits, reducing turnover and fresh oversight perspectives.",5,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Police Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.7,"category":0.8,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-990d5d3555",748,"csa","BOS",11,5,null,"Amend Charter Section 4.109 to state that reappointment must be made within 60 days of expiration or seat will be deemed vacant and seated Commissioner removed from seat.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1d",6,3,null,"Commissioners can remain seated indefinitely after their term expires, as seen with one Commissioner serving since 2001 past expiration.",5,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Police Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.7,"category":0.8,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-eb2412ae43",748,"csa","BOS",11,7,null,"By ordinance, create a requirement that Commissioners receive training within six months of their appointment by experts in the public safety disciplinary process as impacted by the Government Code, City law, and department policy.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1e",6,3,null,"New Police Commissioners lack mandated training on disciplinary processes, limiting their ability to carry out oversight duties effectively.",14,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Police Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.6,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-f5e73f1764",748,"csa","BOS",11,5,null,"Specify, by ordinance, that the Commission hold hearings, and submit periodic reports to the Mayor and Board of Supervisors detailing the status of all OCC recommendations and current cases awaiting action.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1f",7,3,null,"The Police Commission bears ultimate responsibility for timeliness on OCC recommendations but has no reporting requirement to ensure accountability.",5,10,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Police Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.7,"category":0.8,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-273d87a2f9",748,"csa","BOS",11,5,null,"The Board of Supervisors could grant subpoena power to the OCC by ordinance. According to the City Attorney's office, granting subpoena power to the OCC would not be subject to meet and confer.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2a",8,3,null,"OCC lacks its own power to compel evidence or testimony, limiting independence and effectiveness of its investigations.",5,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Police Accountability"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.7,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-04b3cc76ff",748,"csa","BOS",11,5,null,"The Board of Supervisors could grant a limited subpoena power extending only to external matters. This authority would not strengthen OCC's power to compel police cooperation, but would assist the OCC in gathering evidence for investigation in a more timely manner.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2b",8,3,null,"OCC lacks power to compel external witness cooperation or evidence such as civilian testimony or media footage.",5,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Police Accountability"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.7,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-97c559db6e",748,"csa","BOS",11,0,null,"Strengthen the effective power for internal cooperation held by the OCC with an ordinance not only requiring cooperation upon direct request, but including timelines for cooperation and citing a specific penalty for failure to cooperate. According to the City Attorney's office, implementation of this recommendation is, as it affects the basis for disciplinary actions, likely to be subject to...",624,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2c",8,3,null,"SFPD has at times failed to cooperate with OCC investigative requests, and no penalty exists in the Charter for non-cooperation.",1,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Police Accountability","Police Department"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.7,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-bdd8677c26",748,"csa","DPA",11,10,null,"The OCC should be directed to highlight cases, to the extent possible, where the Department or officers are delinquent in responding to OCC requests, particularly where the lack of timeliness will result in dismissal of the complaint. The OCC should also report serious violations of this type publicly to the Mayor and Board.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2d",8,3,null,"OCC's periodic reports are primarily statistical and do not highlight departmental non-cooperation that could result in dismissed complaints.",9,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Police Accountability"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.8,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-cc606716d7",748,"csa","DPA",11,8,null,"At a minimum the Department and OCC should add to the Early Warning System civil rights complaints, civil suits against individual officers, and City settlements as possible indicators of high risk, none of which appear as triggers in the Early Warning System at this time. They should also consider adding items such as use of force reports, firearms discharge, resisting an officer arrests and...",44,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3a",11,3,null,"San Francisco's Early Warning System uses only complaint counts as triggers, missing indicators such as civil suits and firearms discharge used in other jurisdictions.",7,10,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Police Accountability","Police Department"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.85,"department":0.75,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-159a9a3c65",748,"csa","BOS",11,10,null,"The Board of Supervisors could require the OCC, the Management Control Division, and an independent City agency such as the Controller or Ethics staff to come together in a working group to develop and propose changes to the system triggers and resulting interventions within a specific time period, or the Police Commission could come forward with a decision on a more effective system of...",641,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3b",12,3,null,"Current EWS triggers (3 complaints in 6 months or 4 in a year) lack sufficient scope and fail to distinguish complaint severity, missing many problem-officer patterns.",9,8,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Police Accountability","Police Department","Police Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.85,"department":0.7,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-49c10b8ab7",748,"csa","BOS",11,8,null,"The Board of Supervisors could direct the OCC, the Management Control Division, and the Police Commission to form a working group to work under deadline to manage an upgrade to a more sophisticated system for early warning and risk management capable of producing reports at a significant level of detail to enhance proactive intervention, discipline, and trend-spotting.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3c",12,3,null,"The EWS technology is an outdated, oversized Access 2000 database on a slow modem connection unable to generate trend or status reports.",7,10,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors","Police Accountability","Police Department","Police Commission"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.85,"department":0.7,"category":0.85,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-241b1e0f36",748,"csa","POL",11,5,null,"The department should review the Manual of General Orders to assure all policies and procedures agree with current practices—especially as regards interactions with the OCC and timelines for handling complaint and recommendations—and are updated appropriately.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4a",12,3,null,"Most Department General Orders date to 1994 and may not reflect current practices regarding OCC interactions and complaint timelines.",5,0,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Police Department"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.85,"department":0.8,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-8a2d13965a",748,"csa","POL",11,10,null,"The Police Commission should consider requesting quarterly reports from the Management Control Division similar to and in timing conjunction with the reports required of the OCC. This would include general information on cases received from the OCC, length of time pending, and status (pending, under review, pending action, etc.) These reports would also be a matter of public record.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4b",12,3,null,"No public reporting exists on the Management Control Division's handling and timeliness of OCC-referred disciplinary cases.",9,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Police Commission","Police Department"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.85,"department":0.75,"category":0.75,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-e619a61a49",748,"csa","POL",11,7,null,"The department should consider adding a session on the City's whistleblower policies and protections, and other methods whereby officers can report misconduct or wrongdoing, to other mandatory trainings for police personnel. By doing so, the department would send the message to officers and staff that they support the policies.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4c",13,3,null,"Police personnel training does not currently include information on whistleblower protections and misconduct-reporting methods.",14,2,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Police Department"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.85,"department":0.8,"category":0.75,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},false,[]],["K-41c2e9b42f",743,"csa","BOS",10,0,null,"To ensure fiscal propriety and responsibility, the Board of Supervisors should amend the Administrative Code, Chapter 21, by adding a definition of a sole source contract.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"1",18,0,null,"The City has no legal definition of 'sole source contract' in the Charter or Administrative Code, creating ambiguity in oversight.",1,5,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["Board of Supervisors"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.8,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},true,[]],["K-059c85f7e8",743,"csa","ADM",10,1,null,"Change its procedures to require departments to submit all existing sole source contracts for professional services for review within a reasonable time period so that existing contracts can be reviewed under its new guidelines.",null,"agree","OCA agrees with the audit's assessment that the City's past approach to sole source contracting was inadequate.",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"2",8,0,34,"OCA's new sole source guidelines apply only to new contracts, leaving existing sole source contracts unreviewed.",2,5,null,765,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.85,"response":0.55,"target_date":0.95},true,[]],["K-342e520319",743,"csa","ADM",10,1,null,"Work with departments to help them understand the Office of Contract Administration's new requirements and the procedures they must follow to comply with them.",null,"agree","OCA agrees with the audit's assessment that the City's past approach to sole source contracting was inadequate.",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"3",18,0,34,"Departments may be unfamiliar with OCA's newly issued sole source guidelines and procedures.",2,7,null,765,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.5,"target_date":0.95},true,[]],["K-14a202900b",743,"csa","ADM",10,10,null,"Make the new procedures add value to the contracting process by seeking input from departmental and other users through periodic evaluations, customer satisfaction surveys, or focus group discussions.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"4",19,0,null,"There is no mechanism to gather feedback on whether OCA's new sole source procedures are effective or burdensome.",9,1,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},true,[]],["K-5ed470990b",743,"csa","ADM",10,8,null,"Develop a computerized, sole source database that includes all relevant information for each contract, including type of contract, contracting department, name of contractor, award amount, term of contract, summary of work to be performed, and other relevant information. The database should also have the capability to produce summary reports that can be made available regularly or as needed.",null,"partial","OCA disagrees with the report's description of current data gathering techniques, noting it has developed a tracking system for sole source contracts that come through its office (a manual/paper system).",5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"5",8,0,34,"The City has no comprehensive, reliable, electronic data on sole source contracts, including their number or dollar value.",7,5,null,767,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.85,"response":0.55,"target_date":0.95},true,[]],["K-3e786a160d",743,"csa","ADM",10,10,null,"Ensure that it can produce the types of reports that the Board of Supervisors, other City officials, or the public may request, by making inquiries with individuals, departments, Board members and others on what they want to know about sole source contracts.",null,"none",null,5,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"score":2,"why":null},"6",19,0,null,"OCA lacks reporting capability to serve information requests about sole source contracts from policymakers and the public.",9,8,null,null,null,null,null,7,null,null,null,null,null,1,["City Administrator"],null,null,null,null,{"text":0.9,"department":0.9,"category":0.7,"response":0.9,"target_date":0.95},true,[]]]}});
